del operator
--------------

1. Delete a Variable
python# Simple variable delete
a = 10
print(a)        # 10
del a
print(a)        # ❌ NameError: name 'a' is not defined

2. Delete Single Item from List (By Index)
pythonlst = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]
print(lst)      # [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]

del lst[0]      # Delete first element
print(lst)      # [20, 30, 40, 50]
del lst[-1]     # Delete last element
print(lst)      # [20, 30, 40]

3. Delete Multiple Items from List (Slicing)
pythonlst = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70]
print(lst)      # [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70]
del lst[1:4]    # Delete index 1, 2, 3
print(lst)      # [10, 50, 60, 70]
del lst[::2]    # Delete every alternate element
print(lst)      # [50, 70]

4. Delete Entire List
pythonlst = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]
print(lst)      # [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]

del lst         # Delete entire list
print(lst)      # ❌ NameError: name 'lst' is not defined





